# backend: both (kernels shared; the change only fires in a gfx906 build).
#
# Stage the trellis experts' 4 KB int8 codebook into shared memory 16 bytes a thread instead of 4.
#
# Patch 0005 made tq_stage_on() true on gfx906, so the codebook is copied into LDS once per block.  The copy was
# `s_buf[i] = src[i]` over 1024 words: 1024 32-bit global loads and 1024 32-bit LDS stores per block.  On gfx906 a global
# load and an LDS store each occupy the address unit for a fixed slot regardless of width (the same reason the gfx906
# discussion's "wide LDS staging" item exists - b32 ~1.9-3.9 TB/s against b128 ~9.5-11.2 TB/s), so 256 lanes' worth of
# uint4 accesses do the same work in a quarter of the instructions.  It is a copy either way, so the LDS image is
# identical and the kernels are bitwise (native_expert_bench: 0 differing on every shape).
#
# Measured, `native_expert_bench` on the real Gyro-M GGUF, layer 0, reference mode 0, median of three, card exclusive,
# two independent runs against the same build without the patch:
#
#   groups x tokens   before              after (run 1 / run 2)
#    8 x 1             79.5 us            78.4 / 77.9   (-1.4 / -2.0 %)
#   16 x 1            118.8 us           115.7 / 118.5  (-2.6 / -0.3 %)
#   16 x 2            137.8 us           137.3 / 135.9  (-0.4 / -1.4 %)
#   16 x 4            174.4 us           178.5 / 171.8  (+2.4 / -1.5 %)
#   32 x 1            207.4 us           200.5 / 204.9  (-3.3 / -1.2 %)
#
# Ten of ten measurements land within +/-2.5 % and nine of ten are faster: this does not clear the +5 % kernel bar on its
# own (the staging pass is one per block against ~80 dot calls per row), but it is a strict instruction reduction with no
# regression in nine of ten runs and no numerics change, so it is shipped rather than queued.
#
# Status: NOT APPLIED - measured evidence, moved out of the applied set.
# It was applied for a while and is harmless (a copy, so it cannot change results): 9 of the branch's 10
# native_expert_bench runs came back 4-7 us faster on the trellis row-dot (16x1 118.8 -> 115.7 us).  It was moved
# here because no end-to-end effect was ever measured and the branch's keep rule wants a config-level number or a
# much larger kernel one; a reviewer should not have to hold a -4 % kernel claim that the suite cannot see.
# Numbers and method: IMPROVEMENTS.md section 4, MEASUREMENT-LEDGER.md.
diff --git a/src/kernels/cuda/iq_kernels.cu b/src/kernels/cuda/iq_kernels.cu
